32. The Future West African Megaregion

The likely long-term trajectory is not toward cultural uniformity.

It is toward greater network density.

Imagine a future in which:

* major West African cities are linked by high-speed transportation;
* electricity markets become increasingly interconnected;
* digital financial systems operate across borders;
* ports function as integrated logistics nodes;
* agricultural systems become coordinated regionally;
* universities exchange students and researchers at scale;
* digital businesses serve customers across multiple states;
* cultural production circulates throughout the region;
* and migration becomes increasingly urban and networked.

At that point, the West African subcontinent would become not merely a geographic description but an observable socioeconomic system.

