33. Beyond the Nation-State

This does not mean abolishing national sovereignty.

The more plausible model is layered sovereignty.

A citizen can simultaneously belong to:

[
\text{City}
\rightarrow
\text{Nation}
\rightarrow
\text{West African Region}
\rightarrow
\text{Africa}
\rightarrow
\text{World}
]

These identities are not mutually exclusive.

Indeed, contemporary regional institutions already demonstrate the possibility of cooperation among sovereign states.

The future question is therefore not whether national borders will disappear.

It is whether those borders will become less important relative to regional networks.

